is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
The campus DNS resolver on srv1 (10.5.0.4, running ISC BIND 9 / named) has been
misconfigured with "recursion no" in /etc/bind/named.conf. BIND is only
authoritative for the internal zone "jeremysitlab.com" and refuses all recursive
resolution requests for external domain names. Every DNS query for an external
hostname (e.g. google.com) receives a REFUSED response with the flag "recursion
not available," so PC1's browser can never resolve public URLs — pages spin and
time out, exactly as reported.

IP-layer connectivity is fully intact: PC1 can ping its gateway (10.1.0.1),
ISPA's edge interface (203.0.113.1), and the simulated internet loopback
